  "repo_truth": "The fourth fresh review admitted its exact 17-path subject and returned one Required committed-terminal durability finding. The parent accepted it without waiver and produced this exact 18-path remediated documentation-only subject. Committed and rolled-back terminalization now both use rename-no-replace, preserve/refuse every collision or simultaneous suffix, fsync the transaction parent, reverify the exact terminal set, and replay the parent fsync on exact terminal observation. Baseline HEAD remains db503f7a96479775fe25dbb864b9379fd3e61ac8; no Rust, released record, or immutable prior evidence changed. Independently establish correctness rather than trusting the remediation account.",
  "allowed_scope": [
    "Remain read-only and replay all 18 manifest hashes, lexical order, and aggregate before review.",
    "Read the complete revised subject and independently re-review every Option 1 authority, migration, currentness, status, recovery, and API boundary, not only HCM-2.2-ARPR4-001.",
    "Adversarially enumerate published committed under pending across absent/exact/mismatching/unsafe destinations, simultaneous suffixes, terminal rename, parent-fsync crash, and exact terminal replay; also replay the complete rollback state machine.",
    "Return findings first with exact file/line evidence, concrete failure mode, smallest in-scope documentation repair, and missing validation."
  ],
  "non_goals": [
    "No edits, staging, commits, handoff/ledger writes, or user task hops.",
    "No Rust or implementation approval/work, released-record rewrite, immutable prior-record edit, HCM-2.3 work, or adjacent cleanup.",
    "Do not inherit prior reviews' conclusions or the parent's remediation conclusion; derive the whole verdict independently."
  ],
  "tasks": [
    "Invoke the ordered required skills and return BLOCKED on any subject-manifest mismatch.",
    "Determine whether the entire identity graph is acyclic and all result/intent preimages, schema/vector/persistence/currentness/migration/recovery/fault-boundary rules are exact and mutually consistent.",
    "Verify every forward-writer and rollback-recovery crash boundary maps to exactly one recovery class, repeated recovery reaches the exact terminal set, and every collision/non-writer state maps to evidence-preserving mismatch.",
    "Assess whether the implementation plan closes all four original Review 2 findings, preserves fresh GitNexus HIGH/CRITICAL analysis, and keeps all control-pack status/gate/path surfaces consistent.",
    "Return CLEAN only when no Critical, Required, Optional, or Nit finding remains; otherwise return CHANGES_REQUIRED or BLOCKED without repairing the subject."
  ],
